SCARLET SHADOW — THE HIDDEN CANYON OF THE FOUR SECTS
16:9 NEO‑UKIYO‑E MASTERPIECE
(Complete Sect City Layout with Shadow, Scarlet, Onmyōdō & Demon Sects – featuring Hayabusa, Hanabi, Kagura & Hanzo)
1. REFERENCE IMAGE & GEOGRAPHICAL FIDELITY

Take the uploaded Cadia Riverlands regional map as an absolute geographical stencil for the hidden canyon of Scarlet Shadow. This canyon is not on any official map. It is a cartographic lie – a deliberate blank of swirling silver‑grey sumi ink painted by the map’s calligraphers. You must zoom into the northeastern quadrant of the island, approximately 15 miles east of the City of the Dragon, 2 miles northeast of the Sky Arch, within the upper Jade River watershed. Maintain with surgical precision:

The canyon’s position relative to the Sky Arch (south‑west, visible as a faint, translucent gold arc through the mist)

The City of the Dragon (west, a distant cluster of vermilion roofs and golden palace domes)

The Jade River (north‑west, its waters turning a darker, colder jade as they pass beneath the canyon)

The Forbidden Area of Dragon Soul (east, a distant emerald glow through the perpetual mist)

The Sea of Hope (far west, beyond the City of the Dragon)

The canyon entrance is a narrow, almost invisible cleft in the rock marked by two vertical dry‑brush strokes of charcoal ink and a thread‑thin waterfall – the Shinobi’s Descent. Behind this cleft lies a deep, vertical canyon approximately 3 miles long and 1.5 miles wide, with basalt cliffs rising 800 meters on the north and south sides. The canyon floor is at 200 meters above sea level. The entire canyon is hidden by a triple canopy of ancient pines and perpetual low‑hanging mist that the map’s calligraphers have rendered as a swirling void of pale silver‑grey sumi. No roads lead to it. No ships can see it. It does not exist.

The only transformation permitted is a massive increase in detail to render the four sect cities as fully realised, functional layouts with districts, ministries, dojos, armories, barracks, training grounds, elders’ halls, marketplaces, shrines, fortifications, and warrior cohorts. The map must feel like a forbidden cartographic scroll of a hidden nation – as if drawn by a spy who infiltrated every building and mapped every guard post over many years. The result must be crystal clear, geometrically precise, and artistically breathtaking.

2. CANVAS & COMPOSITION

Generate a 16:9 horizontal image (1920×1080 pixels).

The canvas is a vertical cutaway / isometric‑style layout of the hidden canyon. The canyon is oriented north‑south: the highest peaks are at the north end (800m), the canyon floor is at the centre (200m), and the deepest abyss (the Hollow Belly) is at the south end, extending another 500m downward. The composition is divided into five vertical zones (from top to bottom) and three horizontal bands (west, centre, east). Every building, path, bridge, and fortification is drawn with architectural precision.

Canvas zoning (vertical):

Zone 1 (Top, 0‑200px, 0‑800m elevation) : The Northern Peaks – jagged basalt spires. Here lies the Shadow Sect City, carved into the highest cliffs and the spire of Moonlit Blade Peak.

Zone 2 (Upper mid, 200‑450px, 400‑600m elevation) : The Eastern Plateau – a flat, mist‑wrapped plateau on the east side. Here lies the Onmyōdō Sect City, connected to the main canyon by a single bridge.

Zone 3 (Centre, 450‑700px, 200‑400m elevation) : The Canyon Floor and Southern Terraces. Here lies the Scarlet Sect City, sprawling across the floor and up the lower southern cliff.

Zone 4 (Lower, 700‑850px, 0‑200m elevation) : The Southern Cliff Base and the entrance to the subterranean tunnels. Here lies the Sealed Gate to the Demon Sect.

Zone 5 (Bottom, 850‑1080px, below 0m) : The Subterranean Depths – the Hollow Belly. Here lies the Demon Sect – Exiled City, carved into the rock 500 meters below the canyon floor.

Canvas zoning (horizontal):

West band (0‑600px) : Western cliff face, Shadow Sect, main entrance (Shinobi’s Descent), rope bridges to centre.

Centre band (600‑1320px) : Main canyon void, rope bridges, the central void where the four sects can see each other (but rarely interact).

East band (1320‑1920px) : Eastern cliff face, Onmyōdō plateau, Scarlet Sect terraces, hidden zipline to Sky Arch.

The entire composition is presented as a mist‑veiled, rune‑etched, silk‑scroll cartograph – as if painted by a master defector using ink mixed with shadow‑mist and spider‑lily sap. All major landmarks, sect districts, ministries, and character placements are labelled in elegant English cartographic script with gold, silver, crimson, or black shadows depending on the sect. The map has a legend box in the lower right corner explaining the colour coding and sect symbols.

3. STYLE: NEO‑UKIYO‑E WITH SUMI‑E INK WASH (THE AESTHETIC OF THE HIDDEN NATION)

The map is rendered in an uncompromising fusion of Neo‑Ukiyo‑e woodblock aesthetics and Zen Sumi‑e ink‑wash techniques, adapted for a hidden, vertical ninja nation with complete civil and military infrastructure.

Brushwork specifications:

Basalt cliffs and rock faces : Sharp, angular dry‑brush strokes of charcoal‑black and cold slate‑grey, with deliberate “flying white” (kasure) streaks to suggest rough stone texture. Cliff edges are dark and heavy; cliff faces have vertical striations.

Buildings : Precise, architectural strokes – straight lines for walls, curved lines for pagoda roofs, tiny repeating strokes for wooden shingles. Each building is distinct: dojos have large open fronts, armories are squat with smoke vents, elders’ halls have curved, sweeping roofs.

Mist : Soft, bleeding wet‑on‑wet washes of pale silver‑grey and faint lavender, applied with the “bokashi” gradient technique to create depth. Mist is thickest at the canyon entrance and the upper peaks, thinnest on the canyon floor.

Water : The Crimson Petal Basin is a wet‑on‑wet wash of deep viridian and crimson, with individual Higanbana petals painted as single, precise flicks of raised red lacquer. The Jade River tributary is a thin, flowing line of pale turquoise with darker jade edges.

Vegetation : Bamboo groves are rendered as vertical, overlapping dry‑brush strokes of dark green or crimson, with tiny leaf strokes. Pine trees are dark, angular clusters. The Wisteria Curtain Walls are soft, drooping purple washes with tiny hanging blossom clusters.

Paths and staircases : Switchback staircases are drawn as zig‑zag lines with tiny horizontal tread marks. Rope bridges are sweeping curves with thin vertical lines for ropes and tiny horizontal dashes for wooden planks.

Warrior silhouettes : Each is a tiny, masterful single‑stroke figure – ninja are crouched or running, kunoichi have long hair or ponytails, onmyōji have flowing robes, demon thralls are hunched with clawed hands. All are clearly distinguishable despite their tiny size (1‑3mm on the image).

Raised lacquer details (3D texture effects):

Shadow Sect : Matte black lacquer for pagoda roofs, shuriken motifs, and the kanji for “shadow” (影).

Scarlet Sect : Raised glossy crimson lacquer for Higanbana petals, Hanabi’s glaive, and the shrine roof.

Onmyōdō Sect : Tarnished silver lacquer for Kagura’s platform, umbrella ribs, and paper talismans.

Demon Sect : Weeping black lacquer (glossy black with a faint purple sheen) for the Throne of Skulls and the Ame no Habakiri.

Gold : Burnished gold leaf (simulated with raised gold lacquer) for the Sky Arch zipline, the Dragon Altar’s distant glow, and the compass rose.

Parchment base : A cold, moon‑pale ivory washi with a subtle pearlescent shimmer. The edges are deliberately darkened with a graduated sumi‑wash to suggest the hidden, secret nature of the map. The paper fibres are visible as very fine, pale lines (simulated texture).

Texture fidelity : 8K‑grade. Every building, every stair tread, every rope bridge plank, every bamboo stalk, every warrior silhouette, and every glowing talisman must be crisp, tangible, and geometrically sound. No smudging, no warping, no AI deformities.

4. THE NEO‑UKIYO‑E BORDER — THE FOUR‑SECT RELIQUARY

The map is enclosed in a single, exquisitely detailed, 40‑pixel‑wide border that functions as a protective reliquary for the hidden nation.

Outermost edge (4px) : A hairline of tarnished, matte black silver – cold, unreflective, absorbing light. It has tiny, raised points of pale cyan (like distant surveillance magic) at 2‑cm intervals.

First inner register (12px) : A continuous frieze of interlocking sect symbols:

Shadow Sect : A crossed ninjato and shuriken (raised matte black lacquer)

Scarlet Sect : A Higanbana blossom with six petals (raised glossy crimson)

Onmyōdō Sect : An open Seimei umbrella with a yin‑yang centre (raised tarnished silver)

Demon Sect : A demon skull with two serpentine horns (raised weeping black)

These symbols repeat in a rhythmic sequence, separated by tiny rope‑bridge motifs (pale silver).

Second inner register (16px) : A flowing band of stylised mist and shadow tendrils, rendered in soft, translucent silver‑grey and deep charcoal washes (not raised, to create depth). The mist swirls and curls; the tendrils weave through it.

Third inner register (8px) : A line of tiny, individually painted paper talismans (ofuda) – each a white rectangle (2px x 4px) with a single, bold black kanji for “seal” (封). There are 72 of them around the entire border, representing the seals that keep the Hollow Belly contained.

Four corners – ornate compass medallions (each 32px x 32px) :

Northwest corner : Shadow Sect crest – a silver crescent moon behind a black shuriken, with three falling cherry blossom petals.

Northeast corner : Scarlet Sect crest – a full crimson Higanbana bloom with a golden centre, crossed with a curved glaive blade.

Southwest corner : Onmyōdō crest – a silver umbrella open, with a paper talisman floating inside it, surrounded by four tiny stars.

Southeast corner : Demon Sect crest – a skull with two serpentine heads emerging from its eye sockets, weeping black smoke.

Innermost edge (4px) : A sharp, fractured enso circle of charcoal‑black sumi, its stroke broken in four deliberate places – representing the four sects and their fragile, broken alliance. The brush stroke is thick and heavy (8px wide), with a “flying white” texture (kasure) where the brush skipped over the paper.

Border colour palette : Matte black, tarnished silver, pale silver‑grey, deep charcoal, glossy crimson, weeping black, and white (for talismans).

5. THE LANDSCAPE — ZOOMED‑IN, HYPER‑DETAILED SCARLET SHADOW (FOUR SECT CITIES)

5.1 Shadow Sect City – The High Citadel of Night

Location : Zone 1 (Top, 0‑200px vertical), West band (0‑600px horizontal) and extending to the central spire at (960px, 100px).

Elevation : 600‑800 meters above canyon floor. The highest buildings are at 800m (Moonlit Blade Peak).

Architectural style : Black lacquered wood, dark grey stone, minimal ornamentation, sharp angular roofs like shuriken edges, hidden trapdoors, retractable bridges, arrow slits instead of windows. Buildings are carved into the basalt or built on narrow terraces supported by wooden pillars driven into the rock.

District layout (labelled) :

Moonlit Blade Peak (leader’s pagoda) : A razor‑thin spire of black basalt rising from the north‑central cliff. At its tip (800m), a three‑tiered black‑lacquer pagoda with shuriken‑edged eaves, each tier smaller than the last. The pagoda has glowing red lanterns at each corner (tiny orange‑red dots). Hayabusa stands on the topmost balcony (see Character Placement below).

Shadow Dojo (Attack Ministry) : A large, open‑air training hall on a wide terrace at 700m elevation, west side. It has a wooden floor (pale brown wash), no walls, and a low, curved roof supported by eight black pillars. Inside, 12 tiny ninja silhouettes are shown in various training poses – throwing shuriken, sparring with wooden swords, meditating. Training dummies (straw) are visible as small brown rectangles.

Armory of Shadow‑Forged Steel : A squat, fortified building of dark grey stone at 680m, directly below the dojo. It has a low, flat roof with a smoke vent (tiny grey plume). Through the open doorway (a dark rectangle), racks of weapons are visible as tiny vertical lines (ninjato, shuriken, kusarigama). A forge is indicated by a small orange glow and an anvil silhouette.

Obsidian Meditation Hall : An open pavilion at 650m, east side, on a natural rock platform. It has a polished obsidian floor (rendered as a glossy black oval with reflected moonlight). Four tiny meditating ninja silhouettes sit at the four corners.

Elder’s Council Chamber : A circular building at 620m, west side, with a curved, overlapping roof like a turtle shell. Inside, a low circular table with five tiny elder silhouettes in dark robes, seated. A single hanging lantern (gold) illuminates the room.

Signal Tower : The highest point on the western cliff (750m), a square wooden tower with a brazier at its top (tiny orange flame with smoke). Two tiny guard silhouettes stand watch. This is the Defense Ministry – it can signal the other sects with fire (red) or smoke (grey) codes.

Black Bamboo Groves : Dense clusters of dark green/black bamboo covering the lower terraces (550‑600m, west side). Tiny moving silhouettes (ninja practicing stealth) are visible among the stalks.

Outer Guard Post (Shinobi’s Descent) : At the canyon entrance (top‑left corner, 50px, 50px), a narrow cleft in the rock. A rope ladder (thin vertical lines with tiny rungs) hangs down a waterfall (thin silver‑blue wash). Two tiny guards with spears stand on a wooden platform hidden behind a rock outcropping.

Shadow Sect Barracks : A long, low building at 600m, east side, with a row of tiny windows. Sleeping quarters for 20 ninja. Tiny laundry lines with hanging black garments are visible outside.

Shadow Sect Hospital (Healing Hall) : A small building at 640m, west side, with a red cross symbol (tiny) above the door. One tiny medic silhouette attending a wounded ninja on a cot.

Warrior cohorts : Approximately 40 tiny ninja silhouettes distributed across:

Patrol routes (along the cliff paths) – 8

Training in the dojo – 12

Meditating in the hall – 4

Guarding the signal tower – 2

Guarding the entrance – 2

In the barracks (visible through windows) – 10

In the hospital – 1

In the bamboo groves (stealth training) – 4

At the armory – 2

Defense ministry assets : Signal Tower (early warning), Outer Guard Post (first line), retractable rope bridges (can be cut), arrow slits in the cliff face (shown as tiny black slits), hidden trapdoors on the stairs (indicated with small “X” marks).

Attack ministry assets : Shadow Dojo (training assassins), Armory (weapons), Black Bamboo Groves (stealth training), a secret tunnel (dashed black line) leading from the armory to a hidden exit on the north side of the canyon (not shown on the map – only hinted by a question mark).

5.2 Onmyōdō Sect City – The Eastern Gate of Spirits

Location : Zone 2 (Upper mid, 200‑450px vertical), East band (1320‑1920px horizontal). Also occupies a floating platform that hovers over the central void (at 280px, 1500px).

Elevation : 400‑600 meters. The floating platform is at 500 meters.

Architectural style : White stone with silver and gold trim, curved roofs like phoenix wings, floating platforms, paper talismans hanging from eaves, open pavilions, and serene gardens. Buildings are lighter and more elegant than the Shadow Sect.

District layout (labelled) :

Kagura’s Floating Sanctuary : A circular platform of woven silver brushstrokes (approx. 40px diameter) hovering in the air at (1600px, 300px). It is tethered to the eastern cliff by a single, frayed rope of braided white hair (thin white line with tiny twists). Kagura sits on the platform (see Character Placement).

Talisman Foundry : A long, low building at (1450px, 400px) with a sloping white roof and gold trim. Inside, six tiny scribe silhouettes sit at low tables painting paper talismans (white rectangles). Stacks of finished talismans are visible as white piles.

Shikigami Workshop : A small, circular building at (1550px, 420px) with glowing blue windows. Above it, three tiny floating shikigami silhouettes (paper birds with glowing eyes) are shown mid‑flight.

Hall of Purification : A shrine at (1700px, 380px) with a curved, sweeping roof and a central well (tiny cyan circle). The well glows with a soft, steady light. Two tiny onmyōji silhouettes stand beside it, one pouring water.

Elder’s Shrine : A quiet garden (1800px, 450px) with a wooden pavilion (open sides, curved roof). Inside, three elder onmyōji in white robes, seated in meditation. A tiny stone lantern and bonsai tree are visible.

Wisteria Curtain Walls : Along the eastern cliff edge (from 1400px to 1900px, at 380px elevation), a dense row of ancient wisteria trees with drooping purple blossoms (soft purple washes with tiny hanging clusters). These trees hum when demons approach – a natural alarm system (Defense Ministry).

Foxfire Path : A winding trail (thin silver line) from the Talisman Foundry to the Elder’s Shrine, lined with tiny glowing blue mushrooms (dots of pale cyan). Tiny onmyōji patrol silhouettes walk this path.

Bridge of Whispers : The only connection to the main canyon – a long, narrow wooden bridge (from 1320px, 400px to 1000px, 450px) spanning the void. It is drawn as a sweeping curve with vertical rope lines and horizontal planks. Two tiny onmyōji guards stand at the canyon end.

Onmyōdō Barracks : A two‑story building at (1500px, 480px) with windows. Tiny silhouettes visible inside.

Spirit Archive (Library) : A tall, square tower at (1650px, 350px) with a pointed roof. Shelves of scrolls visible as tiny vertical lines through windows.

Warrior cohorts : Approximately 25 tiny onmyōji silhouettes (distinguished by flowing robes and tall hats or hair knots):

Painting talismans – 6

Patrolling the Foxfire Path – 4

Guarding the bridge – 2

Meditating at the Elder’s Shrine – 3

In the Hall of Purification – 2

In the barracks – 6

At the Shikigami Workshop – 2

Floating shikigami (paper familiars) – 3

Defense ministry assets : Wisteria Curtain Walls (alarm), Bridge of Whispers (choke point), protective talismans lining the cliff edge (tiny white rectangles), the floating platform’s height advantage (can see all approaches).

Attack ministry assets : Shikigami Workshop (offensive familiars), Talisman Foundry (sealing and offensive ofuda), the onmyōji’s ability to summon spirits from a distance (indicated by a faint, swirling silver aura around the workshop).

5.3 Scarlet Sect City – The Blossom of Blood

Location : Zone 3 (Centre, 450‑700px vertical), spanning the entire canyon floor (300‑1620px horizontal) and climbing the lower southern terraces (1320‑1920px, 500‑700px).

Elevation : 200‑400 meters (canyon floor at 200m, terraces up to 400m).

Architectural style : Crimson and magenta lacquered wood, gold trim, curved roofs with Higanbana‑shaped finials, open‑air pavilions, bridges over dark pools, lattice windows. Buildings are more ornate than Shadow Sect but still functional.

District layout (labelled) :

Crimson Petal Basin : The centrepiece of the Scarlet Sect – a perfectly circular, dark mirror‑lake at (960px, 550px) with a diameter of 120px. The water is rendered in wet‑on‑wet deep viridian and crimson washes, with dozens of individual Higanbana petals floating on the surface (each a single, precise flick of raised red lacquer). At the exact centre, a small island (20px diameter) with a single, open‑air shrine – a vermilion roof supported by four pillars. Hanabi kneels before the floating Higanbana (see Character Placement).

Higanbana Dojo (Attack Ministry) : A large training ground on the southern terrace (1500px, 600px). It is an open stone platform (pale grey) surrounded by low wooden fences. 15 tiny kunoichi silhouettes are shown training with glaives, chakrams, and throwing petals. Training dummies are painted with red targets.

Poison Garden : A walled garden (1300‑1450px, 650‑700px) with a high stone wall (dark grey). Inside, plants are rendered as dark green and purple clusters with tiny red berries (nightshade), pale pink blossoms (oleander), and massive maroon petals (corpse flower). Three tiny alchemist silhouettes in masks tend the plants.

Crimson Bamboo Fortress (Defense Ministry) : A dense ring of blood‑red bamboo surrounding the entire Scarlet Sect city (from 300px to 1620px horizontally, at 480‑520px elevation). The bamboo is rendered as vertical, overlapping crimson strokes with tiny leaf details. Gaps only at the Main Gate (at 960px, 520px), which is flanked by two stone lanterns with red flames.

Elder’s Pavilion : A raised wooden platform (1400px, 550px) with a large, curved roof of crimson and gold. Three elder kunoichi sit on cushions: one with a staff (a thin gold line), one with a folding fan (a tiny fan shape), one with a tea cup. A low table holds a tea set (tiny dots).

Spider‑Lily Onmyōdō Circles : Protective wards etched into the ground around the Crimson Petal Basin – shown as concentric rings of glowing red runes (tiny repeating symbols). They pulse with a faint red light (rendered as a soft, translucent red halo).

Market Row : A narrow, winding street (1000‑1150px, 600px) lined with wooden stalls (brown rectangles with striped awnings in red and gold). Tiny merchant and customer silhouettes (some in civilian clothes, some in ninja gear) haggle over goods. Stalls sell weapons, poisons, silk, and medicine.

Scarlet Sect Barracks : A large, two‑story building (1100px, 650px) with a row of windows (tiny yellow glows). Clotheslines with red and black garments.

Kunoichi Dormitory : A smaller building (1200px, 640px) with a curved roof and a small garden with Higanbana flowers.

Warrior cohorts : Approximately 35 tiny kunoichi silhouettes (distinguished by long hair or ponytails, some with red ribbons):

Training in the dojo – 15

Patrolling the bamboo fortress – 8

Tending the poison garden – 3

At the market – 4

In the barracks – 5

Guarding the shrine – 2

Meditating at the Elder’s Pavilion – 3

Defense ministry assets : Crimson Bamboo Fortress (impenetrable wall), Spider‑Lily Circles (magical wards), the basin’s reflective surface (can reveal stealth), poison garden (defensive toxins).

Attack ministry assets : Higanbana Dojo (training assassins), Poison Garden (offensive toxins), Market Row (supplies), and a secret underwater tunnel (dashed red line) leading from the basin to a hidden exit on the Jade River (not shown – hinted).

5.4 Demon Sect – The Hollow Belly (Exiled City)

Location : Zone 4 (Lower, 700‑850px vertical) and Zone 5 (Bottom, 850‑1080px vertical). Subterranean, beneath the southern cliff. Accessible only through the Sealed Gate at (960px, 800px).

Elevation : 0 meters (at the gate) down to minus 500 meters (the Pit of Hungry Souls).

Architectural style : Rough‑hewn cave walls, black iron structures, bone decorations, glowing purple and crimson crystals, organic twisted shapes. No wood or paper. The city is built into natural caverns, with buildings carved from stalactites and stalagmites.

District layout (labelled) :

Hanzo’s Throne of Skulls : At the centre of the Hollow Belly (960px, 950px), a crude chair made of fused human skulls (pale white ovals with dark eye sockets, fused together with black iron). Hanzo’s demon entity sits upon it (see Character Placement). The throne is surrounded by piles of bones (tiny white curved lines).

Akuma Shrine : A dark altar (1100px, 900px) made of black obsidian with glowing red runes (tiny crimson symbols) carved into its surface. A brazier of black flame (dark grey smoke with a purple core) burns at the centre. Two hooded demon cultist silhouettes kneel before it.

Flesh‑Forge (Attack Ministry) : A weapon workshop (800px, 920px) where organic and demonic materials are fused. It is an open cavern with a massive stone anvil (grey rectangle) and a furnace (orange glow with black smoke). Three tiny demon‑smith silhouettes (hunched, with clawed hands) hammer at a blade. Racks of demonic weapons (curved, spiked) are visible.

Pit of Hungry Souls : A deep chasm (960px, 1000px) at the bottom of the Hollow Belly. It is rendered as a dark void (pure black sumi) with tiny, ghostly white wisps (souls) rising from it. A railing of black iron (thin black lines) surrounds the pit. Warning runes (red) are carved into the stone around it.

Sealed Gate : The entrance from the Scarlet Sect city (960px, 800px). A massive iron‑banded door (dark grey with black horizontal bars) set into the rock. The door is covered in hundreds of individually painted paper talismans (ofuda) – each a tiny white rectangle (2px x 4px) with a black kanji for “seal” (封). They are arranged in overlapping rows. A single red rope (thin red line) with white paper streamers (shide) hangs across the door.

Corpse Fungus Cavern : A side chamber (700px, 880px) filled with glowing bioluminescent mushrooms (pale green and blue dots). The floor is littered with tiny, slumped silhouettes of those who wandered too close and fell asleep forever.

Demon Barracks : A rough‑hewn cave (1200px, 940px) where demon thralls rest. Five hunched silhouettes with glowing red eyes are visible.

The Maw (Training Pit) : A circular arena (850px, 980px) where demon thralls fight each other. Two silhouettes are shown mid‑combat, with curved blades.

Warrior cohorts : Approximately 15 tiny demon thrall silhouettes (hunched, clawed, with glowing red eyes) and 5 shadow‑winged serpents (coiled on the ceiling):

Guarding the throne – 3

At the Akuma Shrine – 2

At the Flesh‑Forge – 3

In the barracks – 5

Training in the Maw – 2

Serpents – 5 (shown as thin, curved black lines with red eyes)

Defense ministry assets : The Sealed Gate (heavily warded), the Corpse Fungus Cavern (natural trap), the Pit of Hungry Souls (deadly), and the difficulty of navigating the dark tunnels (shown as a maze of dashed grey lines).

Attack ministry assets : The Flesh‑Forge (producing demonic weapons), the Akuma Shrine (empowering Hanzo’s demon), and the demon thralls themselves.

5.5 Connecting Infrastructure & Hidden Paths

Shinobi’s Descent (entrance) : At (300px, 50px). A narrow cleft in the north‑western cliff. Rendered as two vertical charcoal strokes with a thin silver‑blue waterfall between them. A rope ladder (thin black vertical lines with tiny horizontal rungs) hangs down 100px. A wooden platform (brown rectangle) at the bottom with two tiny guards.

Rope Bridges :

Bridge of Whispers : Connects Onmyōdō plateau (1320px, 400px) to the central canyon (1000px, 450px). Sweeping curve, 20px wide. Two tiny guards at each end.

Shadow’s Span : Connects Shadow Sect (600px, 350px) to the eastern cliff (1400px, 350px). High bridge, 50px long. Shown with a slight sag.

Scarlet’s Sway : Connects Scarlet Sect (900px, 650px) to the lower Onmyōdō path (1300px, 600px). Low bridge, 40px long.

Switchback Staircases :

Stair of a Thousand Cuts (Shadow Sect) : Zig‑zag from (600px, 200px) down to (600px, 450px). Each step is a tiny horizontal line.

Petal Ascent (Scarlet Sect) : Zig‑zag from (1500px, 700px) up to (1500px, 500px). Labelled in crimson script.

Secret Zipline : A faint, translucent gold line from Moonlit Blade Peak (960px, 100px) to the apex of the Sky Arch (off‑map, south‑west). Shown as a thin, dashed gold line with a tiny arrow indicating direction. Labelled: “Hidden Zipline to Sky Arch (Shadow Sect only).”

Secret Tunnel (sealed) : A thin, dashed red line from the Scarlet Sect poison garden (1350px, 680px) to the Sealed Gate (960px, 800px). Labelled: “Sealed Tunnel – Do Not Enter.”

