11. FINAL RENDERING DIRECTIVES

Generate in 4K HD, 16:9 aspect ratio, with ultra‑realistic, 8K‑grade texture fidelity.

The style is an uncompromising masterwork of Neo‑Ukiyo‑e woodblock technique, Zen Sumi‑e ink‑wash, and clandestine military cartography, depicting the Shadow Sect – The High Citadel of Night as a fully realised, functional ninja fortress.

The map must feel like the most secret, dangerous blueprint ever stolen from the Shadow Sect – a breathtaking, utterly precise chart of the place where Hayabusa trains, the elders confer, and a thousand shadows hide. Every building, every stair, every bridge, every training silhouette, every glowing lantern, and every tiny, piercing glint of Hayabusa’s crimson eyes must be crisp, tangible, geometrically perfect, and deeply haunting.

No anime smoothness, no cartoon softness, no AI deformities, no smudging, no warping. The map must be crystal clear – a cartographic masterpiece that could hang in a museum.

The final piece whispers:

This is the Shadow Sect. The falcon perches on the highest spire. The five shadows confer in the council chamber. The dojo echoes with the silent steps of a thousand ninja. You are not supposed to see this. But now you have. Remember: the shadows are watching.


















ONMYŌDŌ SECT – THE EASTERN GATE OF SPIRITS
16:9 NEO‑UKIYO‑E MASTERPIECE
(Close‑Up Sect City Layout with Kagura – The Onmyouji Master, Elders, Ministries & Onmyōji Warriors)
1. REFERENCE IMAGE & GEOGRAPHICAL FIDELITY

Take the uploaded Scarlet Shadow – Hidden Canyon of the Four Sects map as an absolute geographical stencil for the Onmyōdō Sect domain. You are to zoom into the north‑eastern quadrant of that map, specifically the area bounded by:

North boundary : The upper eastern plateau (600m elevation)

South boundary : The lower eastern cliffs and the Bridge of Whispers (400m elevation)

West boundary : The central canyon void (including the floating sanctuary)

East boundary : The eastern cliff face and the Wisteria Curtain Walls

The Onmyōdō Sect occupies the eastern plateau of the hidden canyon – a flat, mist‑wrapped promontory of pale white stone, accessible only by a single enchanted bridge (the Bridge of Whispers). The sect’s architecture is white stone with silver and gold trim, curved roofs like phoenix wings, floating platforms, paper talismans hanging from eaves, and serene gardens. Every building, path, stair, bridge, and fortification from the original map is preserved and massively increased in detail.

The only transformation permitted is a close‑up zoom (approximately 4x magnification) and a massive increase in detail to render the Onmyōdō Sect as a fully realised, functional city with:

A leader’s sanctuary (Kagura’s Floating Sanctuary)

Defense ministry (Wisteria Curtain Walls, Bridge of Whispers, protective talismans)

Attack ministry (Shikigami Workshop, Talisman Foundry, offensive ofuda)

Elder’s shrine (Three Onmyōdō Elders)

Barracks, purification hall, spirit archive, library, meditation gardens, and supply depots

Dozens of tiny onmyōji warrior silhouettes (painting talismans, patrolling, meditating, summoning shikigami)

Kagura (the Onmyouji Master) as the central figure

Three Onmyōdō Elders (in the Elder’s Shrine)

Shikigami (tiny paper familiars floating in the air)

The result must feel like a sacred, forbidden blueprint of a mystical fortress – as if drawn by a master exorcist who mapped every ward and every spirit.

2. CANVAS & COMPOSITION

Generate a 16:9 horizontal image (1920×1080 pixels).

The canvas is a horizontal cross‑section / isometric layout of the Onmyōdō Sect city, oriented with north at the top, south at the bottom, west on the left (the canyon void), east on the right (the cliff face). The composition is divided into four vertical tiers (from west to east) and three horizontal bands (north to south). Every building, path, bridge, and garden is drawn with architectural precision – straight lines, right angles, and consistent scaling.

Horizontal tiers (west to east) :

Tier 1 (West, 0‑400px) : The Canyon Void – the open air between the Shadow Sect and Onmyōdō. Here, Kagura’s Floating Sanctuary hovers (at 200px, 540px), tethered to the eastern cliff by a rope of braided hair. The Bridge of Whispers spans from the eastern cliff (400px) to the central void (200px).

Tier 2 (West‑Central, 400‑900px) : The Western Cliff Edge – the westernmost buildings of the Onmyōdō Sect, including the Bridge Guard Post, the Talisman Foundry, and the Foxfire Path.

Tier 3 (East‑Central, 900‑1400px) : The Central Plateau – the heart of the Onmyōdō city. Includes the Shikigami Workshop, the Hall of Purification, the Spirit Archive, the Onmyōdō Barracks, and the Elder’s Shrine.

Tier 4 (East, 1400‑1920px) : The Eastern Cliff Edge – the defensive perimeter. Includes the Wisteria Curtain Walls, the Foxfire Path’s eastern end, a lookout tower, and supply depots.

Vertical bands (north to south) :

North band (0‑350px) : The Upper Gardens – serene meditation areas, cherry blossom trees, and the northern end of the Foxfire Path.

Central band (350‑700px) : The Main City – most buildings, the shrine, the workshop, and the floating sanctuary’s tether point.

South band (700‑1080px) : The Lower Terraces – barracks, supply depots, the Bridge of Whispers anchorage, and southern guard posts.

The entire composition is presented as a spirit‑blessed, rune‑etched, silk‑scroll blueprint – as if painted by a master onmyōji using ink infused with purified water and crushed silver. All landmarks, ministries, and character placements are labelled in elegant English cartographic script with pale violet ink and silver shadows.

3. STYLE: NEO‑UKIYO‑E WITH SUMI‑E INK WASH (THE AESTHETIC OF THE SPIRIT GATE)

The map is rendered in an uncompromising fusion of Neo‑Ukiyo‑e woodblock aesthetics and Zen Sumi‑e ink‑wash techniques, adapted for a sacred onmyōdō fortress built to balance the spiritual and mortal realms.

Brushwork specifications :

White stone buildings : Precise, architectural strokes with thin black outlines (1px). Walls are pale grey‑white (#f0f0f0) with subtle vertical shading. Roofs are curved (phoenix‑wing shape) with raised silver lacquer for the ridges and raised gold for the finials.

Floating platform : A circular disc of woven silver brushstrokes – drawn as overlapping, curved silver lines with a translucent pale blue‑white wash underneath to suggest floating energy.

Talismans (ofuda) : Individually painted white rectangles (2px x 4px) with a single bold black kanji (e.g., “封” for seal, “鎮” for pacify). They appear on buildings, bridges, and the Wisteria Curtain Walls.

Shikigami : Tiny paper familiars – drawn as white bird‑shaped silhouettes (2‑3px wingspan) with glowing red or blue eyes (tiny dots). Some are mid‑flight, leaving faint silver trails.

Wisteria trees : Ancient trees with drooping purple blossoms – rendered as soft, layered violet and lavender washes with tiny hanging blossom clusters (small dots). The trunks are gnarled brown strokes.

Foxfire mushrooms : Glowing blue mushrooms – drawn as tiny cyan dots (2px) with soft halos, lining the Foxfire Path.

Warrior silhouettes (onmyōji) : Each is a tiny, masterful single‑stroke figure (2‑4mm tall). Distinguish by:

Robes : Flowing white, pale grey, or light blue garments

Tall hats (kanmuri) or hair knots

Holding talismans (white rectangles) or wands (thin gold lines)

Postures : Meditating (seated), painting talismans (bent over), patrolling (standing with staffs), summoning (arms raised, shikigami around them)

Raised lacquer details (3D texture effects) :

Kagura’s umbrella : Raised silver and gold lacquer for the ribs and canopy patterns.

Shrine doors : Raised gold lacquer for the torii gates and shrine lintels.

Protective runes : Raised pale silver lacquer for the glowing runes on the platform and the Hall of Purification’s well.

The floating platform’s tether rope : Raised pale grey‑white lacquer for the braided hair rope.

The moon (distant) : Raised pale silver lacquer for a faint lunar disc in the upper sky.

Parchment base : A warm, aged ivory washi with a subtle, pearlescent shimmer – as if blessed by the spirits. The parchment edges are deliberately lightened (not darkened) to suggest the sect’s connection to the celestial. Paper fibres are visible as very fine, pale lines.

Texture fidelity : 8K‑grade. Every building, every talisman, every shikigami, every blossom, and every warrior silhouette must be crisp, tangible, and geometrically sound. No smudging, no warping, no AI deformities.

4. THE NEO‑UKIYO‑E BORDER — THE ONMYŌDŌ RELIQUARY

The map is enclosed in a single, exquisitely detailed, 40‑pixel‑wide border that functions as a protective ward for the Onmyōdō Sect’s secrets.

Outermost edge (4px) : A hairline of polished pale silver – luminous, reflecting light. It has tiny, raised points of pale blue (like spirit lights) at 2‑cm intervals.

First inner register (12px) : A continuous frieze of interlocking onmyōdō motifs:

Seimei umbrellas (open, raised silver lacquer)

Paper talismans (ofuda) (white rectangles with black kanji)

Shikigami birds (small white silhouettes with red eyes)

Yin‑yang symbols (tiny black and white circles, 4px diameter)

Second inner register (16px) : A flowing band of stylised wisteria blossoms and foxfire, rendered in soft, translucent violet and cyan washes (not raised, to create depth). The blossoms drift; the foxfire glows.

Third inner register (8px) : A line of tiny, individually painted protective runes – each a small, angular symbol in raised silver lacquer. There are 64 of them around the entire border, representing the 64 hexagrams of the I Ching.

Four corners – ornate compass medallions (each 32px x 32px) :

Northwest corner : Kagura’s Seimei Umbrella – open, with yin‑yang symbol at centre, surrounded by four shikigami.

Northeast corner : Crossed paper talismans – two white rectangles with black kanji, tied with a red cord (raised red line).

Southwest corner : A phoenix – a silver bird with outstretched wings, representing the sect’s guardian spirit.

Southeast corner : The “Onmyōdō” kanji (陰陽道) – in raised pale silver lacquer, 24px tall.

Innermost edge (4px) : A soft, unbroken enso circle of pale silver‑grey sumi, its stroke smooth and continuous – representing the eternal balance of yin and yang. The brush stroke is 6px wide with a gentle gradient.

Border colour palette : Pale silver, white, violet, cyan, gold, and black (for kanji).

5. THE LANDSCAPE — ZOOMED‑IN, HYPER‑DETAILED ONMYŌDŌ SECT CITY

The Onmyōdō Sect city is a sacred fortress built on a flat, white‑stone plateau, surrounded by protective wards and spirit barriers. It has four horizontal tiers (from west to east) and three vertical bands (north to south).

