11. FINAL RENDERING DIRECTIVES

Generate in 4K HD, 16:9 aspect ratio, with ultra‑realistic, 8K‑grade texture fidelity.

The style is an uncompromising masterwork of Neo‑Ukiyo‑e woodblock technique, Zen Sumi‑e ink‑wash, and deadly kunoichi cartography, depicting the Scarlet Sect – The Blossom of Blood as a fully realised, functional poison‑and‑steel fortress.

The map must feel like the most forbidden, lethal blueprint ever stolen from the Scarlet Sect – a breathtaking, utterly precise chart of the place where Hanabi kneels before the floating Higanbana, the elders confer, kunoichi train, poisons are cultivated, and the crimson bamboo walls keep all intruders out. Every building, every petal, every bamboo stalk, every poison plant, and every tiny, piercing crimson glint of Hanabi’s eyes must be crisp, tangible, geometrically perfect, and deeply haunting.

No anime smoothness, no cartoon softness, no AI deformities, no smudging, no warping. The map must be crystal clear – a cartographic masterpiece that could hang in a forbidden archive.

The final piece whispers:

This is the Scarlet Sect. The Higanbana blooms on the shrine island. Hanabi kneels before it, her glaive beside her. The dojo echoes with the clash of glaives. The poison garden simmers with death. The crimson bamboo fortress stands unbreached. You are not supposed to see this. But now you have. Remember: one petal falls, and so do you.




















DEMON SECT – THE HOLLOW BELLY (AKUMA SECT)
16:9 NEO‑UKIYO‑E MASTERPIECE
(Close‑Up Sect City Layout with Hanzo – The Akuma Ninja, Elders, Ministries & Demonic Thralls)
1. REFERENCE IMAGE & GEOGRAPHICAL FIDELITY

Take the uploaded Scarlet Shadow – Hidden Canyon of the Four Sects map as an absolute geographical stencil for the Demon Sect domain – The Hollow Belly. You are to zoom into the southernmost subterranean quadrant of that map, specifically the area bounded by:

North boundary : The Sealed Gate (where the Scarlet Sect ends and the Hollow Belly begins)

South boundary : The deepest abyss – the Pit of Hungry Souls

West boundary : The western subterranean cavern wall

East boundary : The eastern subterranean cavern wall

The Demon Sect occupies the deepest, most corrupted level of the hidden canyon – a natural cave system expanded by dark magic, located approximately 500 meters below the canyon floor. The sect’s architecture is rough‑hewn cave walls, black iron structures, bone decorations, glowing purple and crimson crystals, and organic twisted shapes. Every building, path, chasm, and fortification from the original map is preserved and massively increased in detail.

The only transformation permitted is a close‑up zoom (approximately 4x magnification) and a massive increase in detail to render the Demon Sect as a fully realised, functional subterranean city with:

A leader’s throne (Hanzo’s Throne of Skulls, with his demonic entity)

Defense ministry (Sealed Gate, Corpse Fungus Cavern, Pit of Hungry Souls)

Attack ministry (Flesh‑Forge, Akuma Shrine, demon thrall training pits)

Elder’s circle (Three Demon Cult Elders – corrupted onmyōji)

Barracks, summoning circles, sacrifice altars, bone chime corridors, flooded tunnels

Dozens of tiny demon thrall silhouettes (hunched, clawed, glowing red eyes)

Shadow‑winged serpents (coiled on ceilings)

Hanzo (the Akuma Ninja) as the central figure, with his demonic entity and the Ame no Habakiri greatsword

Three Demon Cult Elders (in a dark ritual circle)

The result must feel like a forbidden, cursed blueprint of a demonic underworld – as if drawn by a mad cultist who mapped every soul‑draining trap and every hungry abyss.

2. CANVAS & COMPOSITION

Generate a 16:9 horizontal image (1920×1080 pixels).

The canvas is a vertical cross‑section / isometric layout of the Demon Sect’s subterranean city, oriented with north at the top (the Sealed Gate), south at the bottom (the Pit of Hungry Souls), west on the left, east on the right. The composition is divided into five vertical tiers (from top to bottom). Every cavern, building, bridge, chasm, and tunnel is drawn with architectural precision – jagged rock outlines, organic curves for caverns, straight lines for iron structures.

Vertical tiers (elevation bands) :

Tier 1 (Top, 0‑200px, 0‑100m below canyon floor) : The Sealed Gate & Antechamber – the entrance from the Scarlet Sect. Includes the Antechamber of Talismans (walls covered in ofuda) and the first guard post.

Tier 2 (Upper, 200‑450px, 100‑250m below) : The Labyrinth of Flooded Tunnels – a maze of dark, flooded passages with albino leeches and bone chime corridors. This is the defense ministry’s first layer.

Tier 3 (Mid, 450‑700px, 250‑400m below) : The Central Cavern – the heart of the Hollow Belly. Contains Hanzo’s Throne of Skulls, the Akuma Shrine, the Flesh‑Forge, and the Demon Barracks. Hanzo’s demonic entity dominates this level.

Tier 4 (Lower, 700‑850px, 400‑500m below) : The Deep Tunnels – secondary training pits, summoning circles, and the Corpse Fungus Cavern.

Tier 5 (Bottom, 850‑1080px, 500‑600m below) : The Pit of Hungry Souls – a bottomless chasm of dark energy, surrounded by warning runes and iron railings.

Horizontal bands (no strict division – the cavern is organic) :

West band (0‑600px) : Western cavern wall – natural rock formations, iron structures, flooded tunnels.

Central band (600‑1320px) : The main open cavern – throne, shrine, forge, barracks.

East band (1320‑1920px) : Eastern cavern wall – secondary tunnels, summoning circles, corpse fungus cavern.

The entire composition is presented as a cursed, blood‑stained, obsidian‑etched blueprint – as if drawn by a cultist using ink mixed with demon ichor and crushed soul crystals. All landmarks, ministries, and character placements are labelled in elegant English cartographic script with weeping black ink and purple shadows.

3. STYLE: NEO‑UKIYO‑E WITH SUMI‑E INK WASH (THE AESTHETIC OF THE DEMONIC ABYSS)

The map is rendered in an uncompromising fusion of Neo‑Ukiyo‑e woodblock aesthetics and Zen Sumi‑e ink‑wash techniques, adapted for a demonic underworld where the walls weep black ichor and the air hums with dark energy.

Brushwork specifications :

Cavern walls : Rough‑hewn basalt – jagged, angular dry‑brush strokes of charcoal‑black and deep bruised purple. Use the kasure (flying white) technique to suggest rough stone texture. Veins of glowing cyan and magenta (demon energy) run through the rock.

Water (flooded tunnels) : Glossy wet‑on‑wet washes of sickly pale turquoise and dark indigo, with floating leech silhouettes (pale pink segmented shapes).

Iron structures : Precise, sharp lines of matte black and rusted red – cages, railings, chains, the Flesh‑Forge anvil.

Bones : Pale ivory strokes – skulls (small ovals with eye sockets), femurs (thin curved lines), ribs (overlapping arcs).

Glowing crystals : Raised purple and crimson lacquer dots and jagged shapes, with soft halos (translucent washes).

Demon thrall silhouettes : Hunched, clawed, bestial figures (2‑4mm tall) – glowing red eyes, curved spines, long arms. Some are standing, some crawling on walls or ceilings.

Shadow‑winged serpents : Thin, coiling black lines with red eyes and membranous wings (small dark arcs), clinging to cavern ceilings.

Raised lacquer details (3D texture effects) :

Hanzo’s throne : Raised matte black and bone‑white lacquer for the fused skulls.

The Ame no Habakiri : Raised silver lacquer for the serrated outer edge, raised translucent purple for the inner blade, raised gold for the crossguard orb.

Hanzo’s demon entity : Raised weeping black lacquer (glossy with purple sheen) for its serpentine heads and clawed hands.

The Sealed Gate’s ofuda : Raised white and black lacquer for the paper talismans (each a tiny rectangle with kanji).

The Pit of Hungry Souls : Raised pure black lacquer (void) with raised pale cyan ghost wisps rising.

Parchment base : A cold, dark grey‑brown washi – deliberately stained with oily black smears and rusty red blooms (demon ichor and dried blood). The edges are singed (irregular burnt brown borders). Paper fibres are visible as very fine, dark lines.

Texture fidelity : 8K‑grade. Every cavern wall, every bone, every iron chain, every demon thrall, and every glowing crystal must be crisp, tangible, and geometrically sound. No smudging, no warping, no AI deformities.

4. THE NEO‑UKIYO‑E BORDER — THE DEMON‑SECT RELIQUARY

The map is enclosed in a single, exquisitely detailed, 40‑pixel‑wide border that functions as a cursed seal for the Hollow Belly.

Outermost edge (4px) : A hairline of cracked, weeping black iron – cold, sharp, with tiny, raised points of crimson (like dripping blood) at 2‑cm intervals.

First inner register (12px) : A continuous frieze of interlocking demonic motifs:

Skulls (bone‑white ovals with black eye sockets)

Serpent coils (raised glossy black lacquer)

Clawed hands (raised dark purple)

Broken chains (rusty red lines)

Second inner register (16px) : A flowing band of stylised shadow tendrils and purple miasma, rendered in soft, translucent charcoal and deep violet washes (not raised, to create depth). The tendrils writhe and twist.

Third inner register (8px) : A line of tiny, individually painted bone shards – each a pale ivory stroke, 2‑3px long. There are 64 of them around the entire border, representing the 64 souls Hanzo has consumed.

Four corners – ornate compass medallions (each 32px x 32px) :

Northwest corner : The Ame no Habakiri – the demonic greatsword, point down, with a bleeding eye at the crossguard.

Northeast corner : Hanzo’s demonic entity – two serpentine heads, three clawed hands, burning red eyes.

Southwest corner : A skull throne – a pile of skulls with a crimson jewel on top.

Southeast corner : The “Demon” kanji (鬼) – in raised weeping black lacquer, 24px tall.

Innermost edge (4px) : A fractured, jagged enso circle of charcoal‑black sumi, its stroke shattered in five places – representing the five tiers of the Hollow Belly and the broken soul of Hanzo. The brush stroke is thick (8px) with a “flying white” texture (kasure) that suggests tearing.

Border colour palette : Weeping black, glossy crimson, bone‑white, dark purple, rusty red, pale ivory.

5. THE LANDSCAPE — ZOOMED‑IN, HYPER‑DETAILED DEMON SECT – THE HOLLOW BELLY

The Hollow Belly is a subterranean demon city carved into the basalt beneath the canyon. It has five vertical tiers (top to bottom). Every area is dark, lit only by glowing purple crystals, crimson runes, and the hellish glow of the Pit.

5.1 Tier 1 – The Sealed Gate & Antechamber (0‑200px, 0‑100m below)

Sealed Gate (North boundary, 600‑1320px, 0‑80px) :

A massive iron‑banded door at (960px, 40px) set into the cavern ceiling (the entrance from the Scarlet Sect). The door is dark grey with black horizontal bars, 80px wide, 60px tall. It is covered in hundreds of individually painted paper talismans (ofuda) – each a tiny white rectangle (2px x 4px) with a black kanji for “seal” (封). They overlap in rows, creating a dense, textured barrier. A red shimenawa rope (thick red line) with white paper streamers (shide – small white zig‑zags) hangs across the door.

Warning runes : Glowing red symbols (tiny) carved into the stone around the door.

Gate label : “Sealed Gate – The Only Entrance”

Antechamber of Talismans (600‑1320px, 80‑200px) :

A narrow, low‑ceilinged passage (40px tall) lined with stone shelves (grey rectangles) covered in hundreds of additional paper talismans – white rectangles with black kanji. The talismans glow with a faint, residual holy white‑gold light (soft pale yellow halo). This is the only “safe” area in the Hollow Belly.

Two tiny demon thrall silhouettes (hunched, glowing red eyes) are shown in cages (iron bars) – captured intruders awaiting sacrifice.

Iron bell : A heavy iron bell (grey oval) hanging from the ceiling, used by the Scarlet Sect to signal that the demon is still contained.

Antechamber label : “Antechamber of Talismans – The Last Light”

5.2 Tier 2 – Labyrinth of Flooded Tunnels & Bone Chime Corridor (200‑450px, 100‑250m below)

Labyrinth of Flooded Tunnels (West and East bands, 200‑450px, 100‑250m) :

A maze of winding, narrow tunnels (20‑30px wide) carved through the basalt. The walls are jagged dry‑brush strokes. The floor is flooded with stagnant, sickly pale turquoise water (glossy wash). Albino leeches – pale pink segmented shapes (2‑4px long) – float in the water.

Patrol route : 4 tiny demon thrall silhouettes wade through the water, holding rusted blades.

Tunnel label : “Labyrinth of Flooded Tunnels – Home of the Leeches”

Bone Chime Corridor (Central, 400‑600px, 250‑350px) :

A narrow corridor (30px wide) with a low ceiling (20px tall). The ceiling is strung with bone chimes – human femurs, ribs, and vertebrae tied together with sinew. The bones are rendered as pale ivory strokes (femurs = curved lines, ribs = overlapping arcs, vertebrae = small circles). They clatter in the constant geothermal drafts – indicated by small, translucent soundwave symbols (concentric arcs).

Two tiny demon thrall silhouettes patrol this corridor.

Corridor label : “Bone Chime Corridor – The Voices of the Slain”

5.3 Tier 3 – Central Cavern (450‑700px, 250‑400m below)

The Central Cavern (West‑East, 0‑1920px, 450‑700px) :

A vast, open cavern (1200px wide, 250px tall) with a vaulted ceiling (jagged black strokes). The cavern is illuminated by glowing purple and crimson crystals embedded in the walls and ceiling (raised lacquer dots, 5‑15px, with soft halos). The floor is uneven basalt with pools of black ichor (glossy black wash).

Hanzo’s Throne of Skulls (Central, 800‑1000px, 550‑650px) :

At the centre of the cavern (900px, 600px), a crude throne made of fused human skulls – rendered as a pile of pale white ovals with black eye sockets, fused together with black iron (dark grey lines). The throne is 40px wide, 50px tall.

Hanzo’s Demonic Entity : Towering above the throne (900px, 500px), a massive, semi‑amorphous demon form – rendered in smeared black sumi and deep pulsating purple ink. It has two serpentine heads (curved black lines with red eyes) that rise from a hunched torso, and three clawed hands (jagged black strokes with red talons). The entity’s maw is open, dripping thick, black sumi‑ink saliva.

Hanzo’s True Form (skeletal wraith) : A pitiful, ghostly figure (3mm tall) sitting on the throne – a skeletal, horned wraith of ghostly purple‑black ink, with a golden mask (tiny gold rectangle) covering its lower face. Its eyes are two burning red dots.

The Ame no Habakiri : The demon entity clutches a massive, ornate greatsword (60px long) – rendered in raised silver lacquer for the serrated outer edge, raised translucent purple for the inner pulsating blade, raised gold for the crossguard orb (which glows with a red dot). The blade is 3 times the size of Hanzo’s true form.

Throne label : “Hanzo’s Throne of Skulls – The Demon’s Seat”

Akuma Shrine (Attack Ministry – Dark Rituals) (East band, 1300‑1500px, 500‑600px) :

A dark altar at (1400px, 550px) made of black obsidian (glossy black rectangle, 30px wide, 20px tall). Glowing crimson runes (tiny symbols) cover its surface. A brazier of black flame (dark grey smoke with a purple core) burns on the altar.

Three tiny Demon Cult Elder silhouettes (hooded, black robes, glowing red eyes) kneel around the altar, performing a ritual (arms raised). Above them, a summoning circle (glowing red pentagram, 40px diameter) floats in the air.

Shrine label : “Akuma Shrine – Where Demons are Summoned”

Flesh‑Forge (Attack Ministry – Weapon Crafting) (West band, 200‑400px, 500‑600px) :

A workshop cavern at (300px, 550px) with a massive stone anvil (grey rectangle, 20px wide, 10px tall) and a furnace (orange‑red glow, 15px diameter) with black smoke rising. Racks of demonic weapons (curved, spiked blades) are visible as tiny jagged shapes.

Three tiny demon‑smith silhouettes (hunched, clawed, wearing leather aprons) hammer at blades on the anvil.

